  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\bar{X}$ and M.D. be the mean and the mean deviation about $\\bar{X}$ of $n$ observations $\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}, \\mathrm{i}=1,2$,n. If each of the observations is increased by 5 , then the new mean and the mean deviation about the new mean, respectively, are :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "CsMJP",
      "text": "\n$\\bar{X}$, M.D.\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dhptx",
      "text": "\n$\\overline{\\mathrm{X}}+5$, M.D.\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "teWHO",
      "text": "\n$\\bar{X}$, M.D. $+5$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XB7Oe",
      "text": "\n$\\overline{\\mathrm{X}}+5$, M.D. $+5$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $x_i$ be $n$ observations, $i=1,2, \\ldots n$ Let $\\bar{X}$ be the mean and M.D be the mean deviation about $\\bar{X}$. If each observation is increased by 5 then new mean will be $\\bar{X}+5$ and new M.D. about new mean will be M.D.\n$$\n\\left(\\because \\text { Mean }=\\sum_{i=1}^n \\frac{x_i}{n}\\right)\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
